<section id="s-problem" data-code="problem">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Benchmark Trap</div>
<h2>You asked for 1,000 QPS. Your tool sent 146.</h2>
<p>Production LLM deployments are governed by strict Service Level Objectives: Time to First Token (TTFT) under 500ms, Time Per Output Token (TPOT) under 50ms at the p99. To validate these SLOs, engineers reach for benchmarking tools — vLLM Bench, SGLang's benchmark scripts, Semi Analysis's Inference X. These tools are single-process Python scripts built on asyncio.</p>
<p>They work fine at low concurrency. At production scale — hundreds to thousands of queries per second — they become the bottleneck. The tool can't keep up with the server it's supposed to be measuring, so it inflates every latency number it reports. What looks like model degradation is the benchmark itself falling over.</p>
<p>The chart below shows what actually happens when you ask these tools to sustain 1,000 QPS:</p>

<div class="vp">
