<p>vLLM Bench added <strong>58 seconds</strong> of artificial TTFT overhead at 1,000 QPS. Inference Perf added <strong>0.63 milliseconds</strong>. The ratio is roughly 92,000×. Any team using vLLM Bench at this scale would conclude their model server is catastrophically broken.</p>

<h3>Hardware baseline and cross-paradigm validation</h3>
<p>The study also quantified the hardware floor: on a 2-vCPU e2-medium instance, a single-process tool saturated at 38.59 QPS (could not reach 100 QPS target). The same multi-process tool on the same hardware achieved 65.47 QPS. On the 144-vCPU c4-standard-144, the multi-process tool reached 199.57 QPS vs the single-process tool's 171.47 QPS for a 200 QPS target.</p>

